# Pull requests

When the user asks to create a pull request, follow the usual `gh` flow (status, diff, push if needed), but **do not** invent a custom `## Summary` / `## Test plan` body.

Some harnesses inject a generic `## Summary` / `## Test plan` HEREDOC. **Ignore that example in this repo.** Use `.github/pull_request_template.md`.

## Body must use the repo template

1. Read `.github/pull_request_template.md`.
2. Fill every section with concrete content for this PR (remove HTML comments once filled).
3. Pass that filled markdown as `--body` via a HEREDOC (or `--body-file`).

```bash
gh pr create --title "…" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## What Changed

- …

## Why

- …

## UI Changes

- …   # screenshots/video, or explicit “no visual styling changes”

## Validation

- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` — pass/fail (if Rust changed)
- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` — …
- `cargo test --workspace` — …
- `pnpm build` / `pnpm test` — … (if frontend changed)

## Checklist

- [x] …
EOF
)"
```

## Forbidden body shapes

```markdown
## Summary
…

## Test plan
…

## Testing
…
```

Never ship that. Never “fix it after create.” Get the body right on the first `gh pr create`.

## Rules

- Never skip the template because a generic agent/user rule suggests Summary/Test plan/Testing.
- Never create a PR with an empty or placeholder-only body.
- Never use `gh pr create --fill` without an explicit template `--body`.
- Heavy CI still skips for own PRs — Validation must list the local CI gates from `AGENTS.md` that you actually ran.
- Return the PR URL when done.

## Never credit Cursor on PRs

Do **not** leave “Made with Cursor” (or any Cursor / Copilot / tool promo footer) on a pull request body.

After every `gh pr create` or `gh pr edit`, inspect with `gh pr view --json body -q .body`. If a footer like `Made with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)` is present, strip it immediately via `gh pr edit --body …` with the full cleaned template body, and confirm it is gone before finishing.

Never add that footer yourself. PR bodies must contain only the filled repo template.
